1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,315
This video shows you how to hold a pipeline to a schema,

2
00:00:03,315 --> 00:00:05,950
and fill in the fields it asks for.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,598
Security tools often read OCSF, the Open Cybersecurity Schema Framework.

4
00:00:11,598 --> 00:00:14,670
Add a schema from one of its classes.

5
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:19,885
These records are network connections, so the class is Network Activity.

6
00:00:19,885 --> 00:00:22,470
Name the schema network-activity.

7
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:26,604
Profiles add fields for things like hosts and containers.

8
00:00:26,604 --> 00:00:32,480
Tick one, and your records must carry its fields and name it in metadata.profiles.

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:37,209
This pipeline fills none of them, so leave every profile unticked.

10
00:00:37,209 --> 00:00:41,350
Keep depth 2, with the required and recommended fields.

11
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,463
Add it, and save.

12
00:00:42,463 --> 00:00:44,751
The schema holds 78 fields.

13
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:53,043
Back in the pipeline, add the schema to the Produces bar.

14
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,143
One schema finding.

15
00:00:58,143 --> 00:01:02,030
The schema requires seven fields the rows lack.

16
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:06,705
Fields lists them under Not set, each with its type.

17
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:15,272
A Code step fills them in.

18
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:22,525
Network Activity is class 4001, in category 4.

19
00:01:22,525 --> 00:01:26,364
A denied connection is activity 5, Refuse.

20
00:01:26,364 --> 00:01:28,740
An allowed one is 1, Open.

21
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,790
type_uid joins the class and the activity.

22
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,140
Severity 1 is informational.

23
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:38,343
time is the timestamp, in milliseconds.

24
00:01:38,343 --> 00:01:42,470
metadata names the OCSF version and the product.

25
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:49,755
Last, the addresses and ports go where OCSF puts them, in src_endpoint and dst_endpoint.

26
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,808
The rows fit the schema now.

27
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:58,915
Save the pipeline.

28
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:02,248
Check on learning.

29
00:02:02,448 --> 00:02:07,312
Where do you see the fields a schema requires and the rows lack?

30
00:02:11,712 --> 00:02:17,764
In the pipeline's schema finding, and under Not set in Fields.

31
00:02:18,664 --> 00:02:24,704
When you tick a profile on an OCSF class, what must your records then carry?

32
00:02:29,104 --> 00:02:34,384
That profile's fields, and its name in metadata.profiles.

33
00:02:35,284 --> 00:02:36,814
That's Shape your data.

34
00:02:36,814 --> 00:02:40,539
You parsed raw text, transformed it with steps and code,

35
00:02:40,539 --> 00:02:44,864
enriched it from lookup tables, and held it to a schema.
